main/normalisation/

# The full per-event prediction table from Computational Model Analysis:
# every model in the comparison set x every held-out event, ~80 MB, which
# would be the largest tracked file in the repository by a factor of 2.6
# and would be stored again in full on every regeneration (its floats all
# change, so git cannot delta it).
#
# It is left out because it is REGENERABLE, not because it is unwanted:
# the inputs (data/MainUserStudy/P*/P*_events.csv) and the code are both
# tracked and the split seeds are fixed, so re-running the prediction
# reproduces it exactly. The file itself is not deleted - only untracked.
#
# prediction_events_primary.csv, the primary model's one-row-per-event
# subset, is deliberately NOT ignored: a few megabytes, opens in a
# spreadsheet, and is what an event-level question is answered from.
main/data/MainUserStudy/model_figures/prediction_events.csv

# Rhythm-experiment analysis output. Regenerated in full by the Rhythm
# Group Analysis window from data/quiz/rhythm-* and each participant's
# TrialStructure.json, both of which ARE tracked - so this is derived,
# and a stale copy in the history is worse than none: it goes out of date
# the moment a measure changes, and the figure filenames change with it.
main/data/RhythmStudy/group_figures/
